  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="Tag315" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Wynnewood is a defendant in a lawsuit brought by Lazy S Ranch Properties, LLC, alleging water contamination. Since 12/31/2021, Wynnewood conservatively reported a litigation related reserve in its FERC filing, disagreed with the Plaintiffs&amp;#8217; claims, has not accepted any liability and is defending the case in court. On December 7, 2022, the Court granted&amp;#160;&lt;font style="border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in;"&gt;Wynnewood&amp;#8217;s&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#160;motion for summary judgment and dismissed Plaintiff&amp;#8217;s claims of water contamination; however, Plaintiff won its appeal in the Tenth Circuit Court of Appeals. As a result, the case has resumed in the district court as to only those claims that were not dismissed. Trial occurred in April 2026. The jury ruled in Wynnewood's favor, finding that Lazy S failed to prove there is a leak on the Wynnewood pipeline. Lazy S appealed the verdict and filed their opening&amp;#160;brief on August 17, 2026. Wynnewood's response brief is due October 19, 2026. Wynnewood released the litigation-related reserve as of 06/30/2026.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
</xbrli:xbrl>
